# UX Critic Audit Mandate

When executing ux-critic Phase 4 (critique pipeline):

## Mandatory before handoff

1. Read ≥2 files under `pwa/src/` for the target surface or journey touchpoints
2. Log Evidence block in `CRITIQUE_LOG` (see STATE template)
3. Name rejected brainstorm alternatives (not just the winner)
4. Score rubric 1–5 on all five dimensions; avg ≥3.0; impact ≥3 on `crit-*` row
5. Journey ticks: ≥2 tabs in ordered `touchpoints`; read JTBD + hooked-ux skills

## Phase 5 gate

Run before arm:

```bash
python3 tools/cursor-loop/scripts/validate_critique_tick.py . \
  --state-file docs/window-instances/ux-critic/STATE.md
```

Exit non-zero blocks Phase 9 arm.

## Tick modes

| Mode | When | Focus |
|------|------|-------|
| `journey` | Odd ticks | Cross-tab flow from `JOURNEY_BACKLOG` |
| `element` | Even ticks | Single tab from `AUDIT_ROTATION` |
| `validation` | Every 5th tick or shipped crit without outcome | Post-ship critique accuracy |

## Do not duplicate PO

Grep `UI_PROPOSALS`, `CRITIQUE_BACKLOG`, and shipped `ui-*` before writing new `crit-*`.
